# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ChatSpeed local change: dialogs avoid a docked native view
#
# The workflow window can dock a ChatHub page on the right. That page is a
# native child view (a wry web view) composited above the GPUI surface, so a
# dialog centered in the window is painted underneath it and loses its right
# part. GPUI cannot paint over the child view, so the dialog layer has to
# center in the width it can actually cover.
#
# The change adds one presentation field to `Theme`:
#
#   dialog_reserved_right: Pixels   (serde default 0)
#
# and makes `Dialog::render` use `viewport_width - dialog_reserved_right` as
# the centering width: `props.width` is clamped to that area (minus the
# existing margin) and `x` centers inside it. The backdrop still spans the
# whole window, and the zero default reproduces the upstream layout exactly,
# so every other user of the library is unaffected.
#
# ChatSpeed publishes the dock width into that field from `Observer::render`
# (guarded, so a stable width writes nothing) and passes the same width to its
# own centered overlays (confirm dialog, new-task dialog, composer config
# panel). The dock width itself is clamped like the Tauri carrier: at least
# 375px for the page, at least 480px for the workflow UI.
#
# Re-apply this section together with the frameless change whenever
# `vendor/gpui-component` is copied from a new upstream version.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

